# Defect 251, panel 192's R3, 2026-10-05: a comment refuses what a string
# refuses written as itself but the tab, which a comment holds. Controls in a
# comment reach the terminal of anyone who reads the file (Zig refuses them),
# so each is refused, `invisible_character`, its `certain` fix its name,
# `<U+001B>`, the form a diagnostic shows it in: a comment's text changes and
# the program cannot. A carriage return before a line feed ends the line, and
# a lone one is refused; a doc comment is a comment, and so is another
# language's `//`, told for its `//` and for what it holds.

# a tab	is held
#~v invisible_character invisible_character
# an escape <U+001B>[2J and a bell <U+0007>
#~v invisible_character
# a lone carriage return <U+000D> in the middle
#~v invisible_character invisible_character
# a NUL <U+0000> and a DEL <U+007F>

#~v invisible_character
## a doc comment holding <U+001B>
function main()
    print(1)
    # <U+001B>[0m  #~ unexpected_character invisible_character
